---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import Plate from '../components/Plate.astro';
import Duo from '../components/Duo.astro';
import CtaBand from '../components/CtaBand.astro';
import { contact } from '../data/site';

import heroImg from '../assets/images/flock-golden-hour.jpg';
import bowlImg from '../assets/images/eggs-in-wooden-bowl.jpg';
import feedImg from '../assets/images/hands-holding-farm-feed.jpg';
import seaImg from '../assets/images/hero-basket-sea-of-cortez.jpg';
---
<Base
  title="About Orchard — A Farm in San José del Cabo"
  description="Orchard is a small poultry farm in the Mango Fields area of San José del Cabo, producing eggs and poultry for Los Cabos — and open to visitors."
  breadcrumb={[{ name: 'About', href: '/about/' }]}
>
  <PageHero src={heroImg}
    alt="Orchard's laying flock in warm late-afternoon light, one russet hen turned toward the camera."
    eyebrow="About"
    title="A small farm under old mango trees."
    lead="Close enough to the airport to be improbable, and quiet enough that you forget it." />

  <section class="bay">
    <div class="shell ab">
      <div class="ab__lede rise">
        <p class="statement">
          Baja California Sur is dry country. Almost everything eaten in Los&nbsp;Cabos
          arrives from somewhere else.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="prose ab__body rise">
        <p>
          Most of it comes up the peninsula, across the water, or from further away than
          that. By the time it reaches a kitchen here it has been travelling for days.
        </p>
        <p>
          Orchard started from a simple objection to that. There is a stand of eighty-year-old
          mango trees on the edge of San&nbsp;José del&nbsp;Cabo, and underneath them the air
          moves and the ground stays in shade. It is a good place to keep birds. So we do.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Plate src={seaImg} height="clamp(26rem, 62vh, 38rem)"
         alt="A basket of Orchard eggs on marble above the Sea of Cortez at first light.">
    <span class="eyebrow">The distance from here to the table</span>
    <p class="statement">Twenty minutes, most weeks.</p>
  </Plate>

  <Duo src={feedImg} ratio="4/3"
       alt="A double handful of Orchard's own pelleted feed lifted from the sack it was milled into.">
    <span class="eyebrow">What we actually do</span>
    <h2>We hold the one input that matters.</h2>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        We raise laying hens and poultry outdoors under those trees, and we formulate and
        mill our own feed on the farm rather than buying it in — corn, wheat bran, soybean
        meal and scratch grains, with ginger, turmeric, garlic, onion and oregano. It is the
        one input that changes everything downstream, so we would rather control it. No
        hormones are added, and nothing artificial goes into the mix.
      </p>
      <p>
        Eggs are collected by hand every morning, sorted, packed and delivered across
        Los&nbsp;Cabos by us. The shells come out brown, cream, freckled and pale blue-green
        depending on the bird. We do not sort that out. It is the most honest thing about the
        product.
      </p>
    </div>
  </Duo>

  <section class="bay light">
    <div class="shell ab2">
      <div class="rise">
        <span class="eyebrow">On the word &ldquo;organic&rdquo;</span>
        <h2 class="statement">We took it off the site.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose rise">
        <p>
          This website used to describe Orchard as organic. We do not hold organic
          certification, and using the word without it is a claim we cannot stand behind — so
          we replaced it with the things we can: where the birds live, what they eat, who
          makes their feed, and how quickly the eggs reach you.
        </p>
        <p>
          If those things matter to you, all of them are verifiable. You can come and check.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Duo src={bowlImg} flip ratio="4/5"
       alt="Freshly collected Orchard eggs in a wooden bowl, in the grass beneath the mango trees.">
    <span class="eyebrow">Why the farm is open</span>
    <h2>Most people here have never seen a laying hen.</h2>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        Not the children, and mostly not the adults either. We started running visits because
        people kept asking, and it turned into one of the more worthwhile things the farm
        does — school groups, families, birthday mornings, chefs who want to see the flock
        before they buy from it.
      </p>
      <p>
        A farm you can walk onto is a different kind of supplier. It is harder to run that
        way, and it is the whole point.
      </p>
    </div>
  </Duo>

  <section class="bay light-2">
    <div class="shell">
      <span class="eyebrow">The farm, in brief</span>
      <dl class="glance">
        <div><dt>Where</dt><dd>{contact.areaDescription}, {contact.region}</dd></div>
        <div><dt>What we raise</dt><dd>Laying hens, broilers and ornamental breeds</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Feed</dt><dd>Formulated and milled on the farm</dd></div>
        <div><dt>We serve</dt><dd>Households, hotels, restaurants, villas and private chefs across Los Cabos</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Open to visitors</dt><dd>Families and school groups, by appointment</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CtaBand location="about" />
</Base>

<style>
  .ab { display: grid; gap: clamp(1.75rem, 1rem + 3.5vw, 4rem); align-items: start; }
  .ab__lede .statement { max-width: 17ch; }
  @media (min-width: 900px) { .ab { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; } }

  .ab2 { display: grid; gap: clamp(1.75rem, 1rem + 3.5vw, 4rem); align-items: start; }
  @media (min-width: 900px) { .ab2 { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; } }

  .glance { margin: clamp(2rem, 3.5vw, 3rem) 0 0; display: grid; }
  .glance > div { display: grid; gap: 0.35rem 2.5rem; padding-block: 1.35rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--line-l); }
  .glance dt { font-size: var(--t-eyebrow); letter-spacing: 0.24em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--on-light-mute); }
  .glance dd { margin: 0; font-size: 1.05rem; }
  @media (min-width: 760px) { .glance > div { grid-template-columns: 15rem 1fr; align-items: baseline; } }
</style>
